1 विष् विवेष्टि & वे॑षति, I. वे॑वेष्ति, pp. विष्ट॑
stir, bustle, work, be active, not rest (waters);
 serve, attend;
accomplish, finish (food i.e. eat up), overcome, conquer. C. वेषयति
clothe, dress. — उप serve, attend. परि the same, dress (food);
 P.
have a halo (sun or moon).

विशद a. clear, pure, distinct, intelligible;
 tender,
soft;
 dexterous, fit for (—˚). Abstr. ˚ता f.

विशय m. middle, centre;
 uncertainty, doubt, p.
विशय˚वन्त् & विश˚यिन्.

वि॑शल्य a. having no point (arrow);
 having no (arrow-)
point or wound, i.e. free from pain, N. of a man.

विश॑सन f. ई killing, murderous;
 m. sword;
 n. killing
(an animal), cutting up, slaughter, fight.

वि॑शाख a. branchless or having spreading branches,
forked;
 f. आ sgl. du. pl. N. of a lunar mansion, f. ई a forked pole
(also ˚खिका f.);
 n. fork, ramification.

विशारद a. experienced, knowing, wise;
 clever at,
familiar with (loc. or —˚).

विशाल॑ a. extensive, wide, large;
 intensive, great,
important. f. आ E. of the city of Ujjayinī.

विशिख॑ a. having no tuft of hair, bald;
 unfeathered or
unpointed, blunt (arrow);
 m. a (blunt) arrow.

वि॑शिख a. having no tuft of hair, bald;
 unfeathered or
unpointed, blunt (arrow);
 m. a (blunt) arrow.

विशिष्ट a. separate, distinct, marked by (instr. or —˚);
peculiar, special;
 distinguished, eminent, excellent at (instr. or —˚),
best of (gen.);
 different from i.e. better or worse than (abl. or —˚).
Abstr. ˚ता f., ˚त्व n.

विशीर्ण a. broken, torn, scattered, decayed, wasted,
destroyed;
 abstr. ˚ता f.

विशुद्ध a. completely purified or cleansed, pure, clear,
bright;
 settled, absolved, finished. Abstr. ˚ता f., ˚त्व n.

विशृङ्खल a. unfettered, unrestrained;
 immoderate,
excessive, n. adv.

विशेष m. (n.) distinction, difference, special property,
peculiarity;
 kind, species, individual;
 eminence, superiority;
 something
extraordinary of, chief, first rate (˚— or —˚) — Instr., abl., & ˚—
in a high degree, especially, particularly.

विशेषक a. distinguishing, qualifying;
 m. n. mark of the
forehead.

विशेषण a. & n. distinguishing, specializing;
 n. also
doing better, surpassing;
 kind, species;
 the specializing word i.e.
attribute, adjective, adverb, or predicate.

विशेष्य a. what is distinguished or specialized;
 n.
substantive, subject.

विश्प॑ति m. chief of a settlement or a community;
 du.
master and mistress of the house.

विश्य॑ a. forming or belonging to a community;
 m. a man of
the third caste.

विश्राम m. rest, repose, deep breath;
 cessation,
tranquillity;
 also = seq.

विश्रान्त a. rested, refreshed, ceased;
 desisting from, i.e.
destitute of, -less (—˚).

विश्लेषिन् a. getting loose, falling asunder;
 separated
(from the beloved person).

वि॑श्व a. all, every (n. every one);
 entire, whole,
universal, pervading all (Viṣṇu, the intellect, etc.);
 pl. विश्वे
(±देवास्) all the gods or the All-gods (as a class). m. the intellect
(ph.);
 n. the All or Universe.

विश्व॑देव a. all-divine;
 m. pl. the All-gods (cf.
वि॑श्व).

विश्वनाथ m. lord of the universe;
 E. of Śiva, a
man's name.

विश्वंभर॑ a. supporting the universe,
all-sustaining;
 m. fire, E. of Viṣṇu, f. आ the earth.

विश्वसनीय a. to be trusted (n. impers.);
 abstr.
˚ता f.

विश्वस्त a. confident, fearless, trusting in (gen.);
 n.
adv.

विश्वा॑वसु a. blessing all (Viṣṇu);
 m. N. of a
Gandharva, a son of Purūravas, etc.

विश्वास m. confidence, trust in (loc., gen. instr.
±सह, or —˚);
 private communication, secret.

वि॑षक्त a. hung, hanging or sticking in, turned upon
(loc. or —˚);
 dependent on (—˚).

विषा॑ण n. (old also आ f.) horn (adj. —˚ f. आ & ई),
tusk (of an elephant or Ganeśa), claw (of a crab), nipple;
 point i.g.

वि॑षम a. uneven, unequal, odd (number);
 different,
changing;
 difficult, hard, adverse, cross, inimical;
 bad, mean,
dishonest, false, wrong. n. unevenness, bad road, pit, precipice;
difficulty, pain, distress, adversity;
 unequality, incongruency,
incompatibility.

विषयवासिन् a. living in a country;
 m. inhabitant of a
country, countryman.

विषयी@कृ spread, diffuse;
 subdue, make a thing an
object, P. ˚भू.

विषुव॑न्त् a. belonging to both sides, i.e. middle,
central. m. middle day ((r.));
 n. equinox.

विषूव॑न्त् a. belonging to both sides, i.e. middle,
central. m. middle day ((r.));
 n. equinox.

विष्कम्भ m. support;
 width, diameter;
 also = seq. m.

विष्कम्भक a. supporting;
 m. a kind of interlude or
introductory scene (d.).

विष्ट॑ a. entered etc., contained in (acc. or loc.);
 filled
or joined with (instr.).

वि॑ष्टब्ध a. fixed, firm (also वि॑ष्टभित);
supported, stayed, stopped, hindered;
 stiff, rigid, motionless.

विष्ट॑म्भन f. ई supporting;
 n. obstruction,
suppression.

विष्टि॑ f. bustle, stirring, activity, service;
 one's turn,
times (—˚).

1 विष्ठा॑ f. place, province, domain, division, party;
 kind,
form.

वि॑ष्ठित a. standing asunder, scattered, diffused,
spread;
 fixed, standing or being in (loc. or —˚).

वि॑ष्वञ्च् f. वि॑षूची turned to or being on both (all)
sides;
 going asunder, splitting, spreading everywhere;
 diverging, averse
or separated from (abl. or instr.). n. विष्वक् adv. sideways, all
around, everywhere.

विष्वद्र्यञ्च् a. turned everywhere;
 n. द्र्य॑क्
sideways, away.

विसर्ग॑ m. cessation, end;
 loosening, letting go;
dismission, evacuation (of the body);
 gift, donation;
 hurling, throwing,
casting, shooting off;
 production, creation (abstr. & concr.);
 a kind of
aspiration & its sign (g.).

विस॑र्जन n. cessation, end;
 making cease, remove;
letting go, dismission etc. = prec. as far as creation.

विसर्पण a. & n. spreading, increasing;
 n. also moving
off, budging.

वि॑सर्पिन् a. springing forth, coming out of (—˚);
 moving
to and fro, spreading, expanding.

विसृत a. expanded, stretched, slackened (bowstring), gone
asunder;
 come forth or sprung from (—˚);
 prominent (eyes).

विस्तर a. extensive. m. extent, width;
 spreading,
expanding;
 abundance, multitude, completeness, prolixity, specification.
Instr., abl., विस्तर˚तस् & विस्तर˚शस् adv. diffusely, fully, in
detail.

विस्तीर्ण a. strewed, scattered, covered;
 spread,
expanded, developed, broad, wide, ample, numerous, far-sounding.

विस्तृत a. strewed, scattered, covered;
 spread, expanded,
developed, broad, wide, ample, numerous, far-sounding.

विस्पष्ट a. visible, clear, distinct, intelligible;
 n.
adv.

विस्फार m. gaping, bursting, opening;
 the twang of a
bow-string.

विस्मृत a. having forgotten (acc. or —˚);
 being forgotten
by (instr. or gen.).
